WEBVTT

00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:05.150
Kaze ni kami ga nabiku

00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:05.150
My hair flows in the wind.

00:00:05.150 --> 00:00:10.720
Kokoro ni hirogaru aozora no deai

00:00:05.150 --> 00:00:10.720
An encounter in the blue skies of our hearts...

00:00:11.290 --> 00:00:15.980
Tooku hanaretetemo

00:00:11.290 --> 00:00:15.980
Though we are apart,

00:00:15.980 --> 00:00:21.590
Kanjiru koto wa itsumo kimi dakara

00:00:15.980 --> 00:00:21.590
I'm always thinking about you,

00:00:21.590 --> 00:00:26.930
Itsu no hi ka mune wo hatte

00:00:21.590 --> 00:00:26.930
so let's promise to meet again

00:00:26.930 --> 00:00:32.410
Au koto wo yakusoku shiyou

00:00:26.930 --> 00:00:32.410
one day, with our heads held high.

00:00:32.410 --> 00:00:39.020
Zutto futari owari no nai

00:00:32.410 --> 00:00:39.020
We'll be together, like a dream

00:00:39.020 --> 00:00:45.410
Yume wo egaku you ni

00:00:39.020 --> 00:00:45.410
with no end.

00:00:45.410 --> 00:00:47.440
Kimi ni

00:00:45.410 --> 00:00:47.440
I want

00:00:47.440 --> 00:00:56.400
Kono omoi itsu no hi ka tsutaetai

00:00:47.440 --> 00:00:56.400
to tell you this someday.

00:00:58.180 --> 00:01:07.370
Sabishisa wo shiawase ni kaeru tame

00:00:58.180 --> 00:01:07.370
I'm right here next to you

00:01:09.140 --> 00:01:16.460
Soba ni iru yo kokoro wa

00:01:09.140 --> 00:01:16.460
to turn your loneliness into joy.

00:01:17.380 --> 00:01:24.830
Konna ni chikaku ni kanjiru

00:01:17.380 --> 00:01:24.830
I can feel your heart so close to mine.

00:01:32.770 --> 00:01:38.540
The only way Maya Kitajima can return to her mentor,

00:01:38.540 --> 00:01:44.890
the once-revered actress Chigusa Tsukikage, is to win the role...

00:01:44.890 --> 00:01:48.660
of Helen Keller, in Daito Theater's season opener <i>The Miracle Worker</i>.

00:01:48.660 --> 00:01:57.200
Among the contenders for the role of Helen is Maya's eternal arch-rival,

00:01:57.200 --> 00:02:01.100
Ayumi Himekawa.

00:02:01.120 --> 00:02:06.080
Episode 22 - The Miracle Worker: The Final Round

00:02:21.270 --> 00:02:23.800
This is the first time Ayumi Himekawa and Utako Himekawa...

00:02:23.800 --> 00:02:26.320
have seen each other in a month!

00:02:26.960 --> 00:02:28.980
They didn't even make eye-contact when they saw each other!

00:02:28.980 --> 00:02:30.720
So, when it comes to the acting world, they haven't even met yet, huh?

00:02:30.720 --> 00:02:32.390
What a weird relationship.

00:02:32.720 --> 00:02:35.030
Miss Rena Shiratori, please come in.

00:02:37.320 --> 00:02:41.060
Please close the door and entertain yourself as Helen for a while.

00:02:41.870 --> 00:02:43.260
You want me to entertain myself as Helen?

00:02:46.790 --> 00:02:49.260
Miss Akiko Hayakawa, please come in.

00:02:52.790 --> 00:02:54.680
You want me to entertain myself as Helen?

00:02:57.150 --> 00:02:59.720
Miss Emi Kanaya, please come in.

00:03:32.390 --> 00:03:36.180
You must confirm the nature of the objects around you through biting.

00:03:36.180 --> 00:03:38.600
That's how they find out about their world.

00:03:44.550 --> 00:03:47.580
She's enjoying the beat pulsing through her hand!

00:03:48.250 --> 00:03:51.480
She's trying to use all the toys!

00:03:51.890 --> 00:03:55.210
It's rare to find such gripping acting!

00:03:55.210 --> 00:03:57.460
She has a wonderful confidence in the role.

00:04:02.010 --> 00:04:04.110
Miss Ayumi Himekawa.

00:04:05.750 --> 00:04:08.810
Please entertain yourself with these toys as though you are Helen.

00:04:08.810 --> 00:04:10.130
Okay.

00:04:21.900 --> 00:04:24.740
Is she acting?

00:04:24.740 --> 00:04:27.200
No, this is what Helen would do.

00:04:27.200 --> 00:04:32.180
Helen can't see or hear, so she wouldn't know that there are toys spread out around her.

00:04:32.180 --> 00:04:34.560
But even so, we should...

00:04:35.220 --> 00:04:35.920
Go ahead.

00:04:35.920 --> 00:04:37.190
It doesn't matter.

00:04:38.620 --> 00:04:39.930
Oh no!

00:04:44.730 --> 00:04:46.140
Did you see that?

00:04:46.140 --> 00:04:49.500
She didn't even flinch or dodge!

00:04:53.550 --> 00:04:54.880
We'll stop right there.

00:04:56.420 --> 00:04:57.890
Thank you.

00:05:10.710 --> 00:05:15.360
If you can't play as Helen, you won't be able to grasp the real Helen.

00:05:16.200 --> 00:05:20.970
Miss Maya Kitajima. We would like you to entertain yourself as though you are Helen.

00:05:21.390 --> 00:05:25.880
The act of playing in a world of darkness and silence.

00:05:38.450 --> 00:05:40.470
What are you doing?

00:05:40.970 --> 00:05:44.840
Didn't you understand our instructions? You have to play like Helen would!

00:05:53.090 --> 00:05:55.480
Observe her expression! Her gestures!

00:05:59.300 --> 00:06:01.900
She really is playing as though she is Helen.

00:06:03.560 --> 00:06:06.340
That's right. Helen can't see or hear, so she wouldn't realize...

00:06:06.340 --> 00:06:09.380
that there are toys around her.

00:06:09.380 --> 00:06:13.250
What you are witnessing is probably what Helen would really have done.

00:06:16.190 --> 00:06:21.200
The first round is over. What will they ask us to do next?

00:06:22.090 --> 00:06:23.830
Thank you for waiting.

00:06:23.830 --> 00:06:25.510
We've prepared lunch for you.

00:06:26.260 --> 00:06:28.240
Please help yourselves to the food.

00:06:28.240 --> 00:06:30.670
However, this is also the second round of the audition.

00:06:30.670 --> 00:06:32.600
We would like you to eat your meal as Helen.

00:06:33.250 --> 00:06:35.210
Eating as Helen?

00:06:35.210 --> 00:06:38.600
She can't hear or see...

00:07:03.470 --> 00:07:06.090
They're acting like dogs... or cats even!

00:07:06.090 --> 00:07:09.940
Yes, but before Helen Keller met Annie Sullivan,

00:07:09.940 --> 00:07:12.870
she was described as a wild animal.

00:07:12.870 --> 00:07:14.930
Isn't that correct?

00:07:41.260 --> 00:07:43.750
What a ludicrous sight...

00:07:47.560 --> 00:07:48.690
And stop!

00:07:48.690 --> 00:07:50.820
This ends the second round of the auditions.

00:07:51.260 --> 00:07:55.810
Miss Ayumi, can you tell us why you chose the curry first?

00:07:56.270 --> 00:07:58.820
Because of its strong smell.

00:07:59.350 --> 00:08:01.490
But after you tasted it, you spat it straight back out, didn't you?

00:08:01.490 --> 00:08:02.190
Why did you do that?

00:08:02.750 --> 00:08:05.380
Because I didn't know it would be spicy.

00:08:07.040 --> 00:08:09.710
Are there any more questions?

00:08:09.710 --> 00:08:11.300
If not, please excuse me.

00:08:13.430 --> 00:08:14.790
Did you hear that?

00:08:15.290 --> 00:08:18.920
Only Helen would have said something like that.

00:08:19.650 --> 00:08:23.140
Only someone who had become her in both body and soul.

00:08:23.140 --> 00:08:24.640
What do you mean?

00:08:24.640 --> 00:08:30.670
Helen couldn't see nor hear, so she wouldn't know it was curry...

00:08:30.670 --> 00:08:32.910
nor that it was spicy until she put it in her mouth.

00:08:32.910 --> 00:08:35.180
That's why she spat it out. She was shocked by its taste.

00:08:35.780 --> 00:08:39.760
There's no doubt about it. She's frightening, that one.

00:08:39.760 --> 00:08:42.950
Ayumi Himekawa is all but perfect.

00:08:42.950 --> 00:08:45.980
Emi Kanaya gives the role a fascinating twist.

00:08:46.370 --> 00:08:50.800
Compared to her, Rena Shiratori and Akiko Hayakawa have been...

00:08:50.800 --> 00:08:53.010
no more than average.

00:08:53.490 --> 00:08:57.950
And then, there's that animalistic girl, Maya Kitajima.

00:08:57.950 --> 00:09:00.760
She has a certain appeal to her.

00:09:04.410 --> 00:09:07.750
And now, we shall commence the third round.

00:09:07.750 --> 00:09:09.970
We would like you to act out the way Helen looks for her mother after...

00:09:09.970 --> 00:09:11.140
waking up from a nap.

00:09:11.950 --> 00:09:14.120
That will be your next task.

00:09:21.880 --> 00:09:28.170
"He didn't defeat us in Vicksburg; we defeated ourselves by making grave tactical errors!"

00:09:29.770 --> 00:09:33.140
The repeated rehearsals seem to have paid off for both Shiratori and Hayakawa.

00:09:33.140 --> 00:09:34.780
They're doing very well.

00:09:36.240 --> 00:09:38.850
"And what do you know about it, James?"

00:09:38.850 --> 00:09:43.230
"Father, wait! Hear me out!"

00:09:43.230 --> 00:09:47.050
The gestures she's making in looking for her mother are quite detailed...

00:09:47.050 --> 00:09:48.420
sometimes even bold.

00:09:48.990 --> 00:09:51.180
"He's nothing but a drunkard!"

00:09:51.180 --> 00:09:54.380
"No, and he won't just roll over!"

00:09:54.380 --> 00:09:56.390
"When he attacked Vicksburg..."

00:09:58.570 --> 00:10:01.090
What are you doing, little miss?

00:10:02.830 --> 00:10:06.290
She's getting agitated because she can't find her mother.

00:10:06.290 --> 00:10:07.490
She's good.

00:10:07.490 --> 00:10:09.810
That's a very bold expression!

00:10:15.720 --> 00:10:19.050
Her acting really fills the stage. It's very dynamic.

00:10:47.920 --> 00:10:49.240
She's very good.

00:10:49.240 --> 00:10:51.890
You can sense her disappointment, when she realizes...

00:10:51.890 --> 00:10:54.410
that her mother's not on the couch.

00:10:54.930 --> 00:11:00.940
"He didn't defeat us in Vicksburg; we defeated ourselves by making grave tactical errors!"

00:11:01.850 --> 00:11:04.680
"But Father, if you ask me..."

00:11:04.680 --> 00:11:07.520
"And what do you know about it, James?"

00:11:09.690 --> 00:11:13.690
"Father, wait! Hear me out!"

00:11:13.690 --> 00:11:18.180
"The reason we lost Vicksburg is because he had resources...

00:11:18.180 --> 00:11:20.470
the other battalions did not."

00:11:20.470 --> 00:11:22.130
"He's nothing but a drunkard!"

00:11:22.130 --> 00:11:27.340
"No, and he won't just roll over! When he attacked Vicksburg..."

00:11:43.970 --> 00:11:47.270
Ayumi really is a genius!

00:11:47.270 --> 00:11:49.460
I have to beat her out for the role?

00:11:53.470 --> 00:11:55.980
Ayumi Himekawa's very good, isn't she?

00:11:55.980 --> 00:12:00.540
She's using that doll to great effect to show her psychological state.

00:12:01.160 --> 00:12:04.760
Masumi Hayami is watching too.

00:12:04.760 --> 00:12:09.530
If I fail now, it'll play right into his hands.

00:12:09.530 --> 00:12:13.960
If I lose this fight, I'll never stand on the stage again.

00:12:13.960 --> 00:12:19.110
I can't lose. I have to do this, for my one true fan, Mr. Purple Roses!

00:12:22.420 --> 00:12:25.150
It doesn't matter if this is only an audition.

00:12:25.560 --> 00:12:30.550
This is still a stage and I'm going to put on Helen's mask.

00:12:31.820 --> 00:12:36.280
I am Helen. I am Helen Keller!

00:12:38.570 --> 00:12:41.730
"We defeated ourselves by making grave tactical errors!"

00:12:41.730 --> 00:12:44.490
"But Father, if you ask me..."

00:12:44.490 --> 00:12:46.200
"And what do you know about it, James?"

00:12:46.200 --> 00:12:50.450
"Father, wait! Hear me out!"

00:13:03.790 --> 00:13:07.390
"What are you doing, Miss Helen?"

00:13:10.130 --> 00:13:12.800
What a wonderful smile.

00:13:39.920 --> 00:13:44.260
I was really taken aback by Maya Kitajima's expression.

00:13:44.260 --> 00:13:48.970
However, this is really between Ayumi Himekawa and Emi Kanaya.

00:13:48.970 --> 00:13:53.330
Ayumi's genius or Kanaya's dynamic style.

00:13:53.330 --> 00:13:56.130
However, the real problem is the upcoming final round.

00:13:56.130 --> 00:13:59.350
We don't know if any of them will pass that test.

00:13:59.350 --> 00:14:01.730
I would now like to announce the final round of the auditions.

00:14:01.730 --> 00:14:06.820
I'm going to call the judges now. As Helen, please wait here until they arrive.

00:14:08.040 --> 00:14:10.720
The final round of the auditions.

00:14:10.720 --> 00:14:15.430
If I don't win this, I'm going to have to leave Ms. Tsukikage.

00:14:16.040 --> 00:14:17.800
You'll be expelled!

00:14:18.250 --> 00:14:21.620
This may be my last chance to become Helen.

00:14:27.750 --> 00:14:29.100
What's going on?

00:14:29.100 --> 00:14:30.800
What happened?

00:14:36.490 --> 00:14:39.390
This is unbelievable.

00:14:44.870 --> 00:14:47.620
Thank you. That was the final round.

00:14:48.090 --> 00:14:49.750
What do you mean?

00:14:49.750 --> 00:14:52.580
The fire alarm was the final round.

00:14:52.580 --> 00:14:56.820
When I left the room, I told you to wait here as though you were Helen.

00:14:58.210 --> 00:15:05.190
Any normal person would reflexively respond to an emergency bell,

00:15:05.190 --> 00:15:07.830
except for the real Helen.

00:15:07.830 --> 00:15:11.440
Or someone capable of playing her.

00:15:11.840 --> 00:15:15.170
There was an audition for the role of Helen in the United States once,

00:15:15.170 --> 00:15:17.260
and out of all those auditioning, only one girl...

00:15:17.260 --> 00:15:19.700
didn't turn around when there was a loud noise in the room.

00:15:19.700 --> 00:15:23.820
She went on to receive rave reviews for her portrayal of Helen and became...

00:15:23.820 --> 00:15:25.920
an award-winning actress at the age of sixteen.

00:15:26.430 --> 00:15:31.690
We never dreamed that we would find <i>two</i> girls who would do the same here.

00:15:32.220 --> 00:15:35.510
Oh, so that was the final round.

00:15:35.510 --> 00:15:40.180
I was just thinking that this might be my final chance to become Helen.

00:15:40.690 --> 00:15:46.020
And then, I suddenly felt very Zen and forgot all about being Maya Kitajima.

00:15:46.020 --> 00:15:51.090
I heard the noise, but it didn't make me feel anything.

00:15:51.090 --> 00:15:53.840
It didn't make me want to turn around.

00:15:53.840 --> 00:15:56.520
And you, Miss Himekawa?

00:15:56.920 --> 00:16:02.050
I had become Helen because you told me to wait as her.

00:16:02.550 --> 00:16:05.210
Even though it was a real alarm?

00:16:05.210 --> 00:16:08.640
Yes. Nobody told me to stop.

00:16:09.750 --> 00:16:11.110
I lost.

00:16:11.110 --> 00:16:15.140
My research was perfect and my acting was measured throughout.

00:16:15.140 --> 00:16:21.030
However, I forgot all about Helen's heart and soul.

00:16:21.030 --> 00:16:23.560
I could never really lose myself in her.

00:16:23.560 --> 00:16:26.510
How can you even compare Maya Kitajima's acting...

00:16:26.510 --> 00:16:29.170
to Ayumi Himekawa's perfection?

00:16:29.170 --> 00:16:30.780
We can't put a no-name actress like her...

00:16:30.780 --> 00:16:33.920
on stage for a production as important as this!

00:16:33.920 --> 00:16:36.060
I completely agree.

00:16:36.060 --> 00:16:41.650
The box office would also benefit from Ayumi Himekawa's star-quality.

00:16:41.650 --> 00:16:45.580
Excuse me, but if that's the case, what exactly was the point of the audition?

00:16:45.580 --> 00:16:48.160
That Kitajima girl's acting has a strange pull to it.

00:16:48.160 --> 00:16:52.280
It's almost as if we could expect a new Helen to be born from her portrayal.

00:16:52.280 --> 00:16:55.240
Well, I also liked the animalistic aspect of her acting.

00:16:55.240 --> 00:16:56.640
Excuse me, but did you say <i>expect</i>?

00:16:56.640 --> 00:16:58.170
We're not talking about expectations here, but actual results!

00:16:58.170 --> 00:17:00.300
We are in business, after all. We can't afford to take risks!

00:17:00.300 --> 00:17:01.940
Can everyone please calm down!

00:17:03.300 --> 00:17:05.440
Get as worked up about it as you like.

00:17:05.440 --> 00:17:07.970
The production manager and Director Nishiwaki are with me on this one.

00:17:08.330 --> 00:17:10.760
Not to mention her mother, Utako.

00:17:10.760 --> 00:17:13.750
That makes four out of seven who have picked Ayumi Himekawa.

00:17:13.750 --> 00:17:15.820
The result has been decided.

00:17:21.630 --> 00:17:26.380
I don't think I've ever felt this nervous before.

00:17:26.380 --> 00:17:29.580
It's that girl... she's making me nervous.

00:17:30.110 --> 00:17:33.390
She's the cause of all the butterflies in my chest...

00:17:33.390 --> 00:17:37.130
even though she looks like she can't do anything!

00:17:37.130 --> 00:17:40.130
She's even making <i>me</i> nervous!

00:17:42.190 --> 00:17:44.050
Well, this is interesting.

00:17:44.050 --> 00:17:47.380
Will Mrs. Himekawa vote for her daughter because she's family,

00:17:47.380 --> 00:17:51.270
or do the exact opposite to avoid being perceived as biased?

00:17:51.270 --> 00:17:54.540
How could you even suggest such a thing?!

00:17:54.540 --> 00:17:57.550
Yes, Ayumi is my daughter.

00:17:57.550 --> 00:17:59.760
But when we're acting, that doesn't matter.

00:17:59.760 --> 00:18:04.720
If I picked her because I'm her mother, she'd never forgive me.

00:18:05.670 --> 00:18:09.960
As Annie Sullivan, I would like to announce who should play the role of Helen!

00:18:14.710 --> 00:18:17.710
I would now like to announce the results of the final round.

00:18:18.640 --> 00:18:21.980
The role of Helen Keller in <i>The Miracle Worker</i> goes to...

00:18:22.310 --> 00:18:24.410
Ayumi Himekawa!

00:18:26.810 --> 00:18:30.170
And Maya Kitajima!

00:18:30.170 --> 00:18:33.290
We have decided to cast both actresses for the role!

00:18:33.290 --> 00:18:36.020
I've been cast with Ayumi for the same role?

00:18:36.850 --> 00:18:38.940
I've been cast with <i>her</i>?

00:18:39.670 --> 00:18:43.520
We would like you to alternate for the part of Helen.

00:18:45.510 --> 00:18:49.520
Ayumi Himekawa will produce a perfect Helen.

00:18:50.140 --> 00:18:51.980
On the other hand,

00:18:51.980 --> 00:18:56.230
we are expecting Maya Kitajima to give birth to a new interpretation of Helen.

00:18:56.230 --> 00:19:00.700
As Annie Sullivan, I didn't want to cut either actress and I decided...

00:19:00.700 --> 00:19:04.010
that choosing both of them for the role was the most impartial choice!

00:19:07.390 --> 00:19:09.890
Congratulations.

00:19:10.370 --> 00:19:13.820
This is a very important opener for our theater.

00:19:13.820 --> 00:19:15.440
I hope you'll give it your all.

00:19:15.440 --> 00:19:19.500
You bet I'm gonna give it my all, just so Mr. Hayami Jr. won't mock me!

00:19:20.010 --> 00:19:22.510
Why don't you look at me when you talk to me, little one?

00:19:22.910 --> 00:19:26.760
The President of the Daito Theater is talking to you.

00:19:26.760 --> 00:19:28.200
In the world of acting,

00:19:28.200 --> 00:19:31.270
you could say that good breeding is more important than acting technique.

00:19:31.270 --> 00:19:33.630
You can hate me all you like.

00:19:33.630 --> 00:19:38.230
But if you want to make it in this world, keep it under wraps.

00:19:38.230 --> 00:19:40.490
Especially around people involved in the production.

00:19:41.820 --> 00:19:45.190
I hear they've already started rehearsing for <i>The Miracle Worker</i>.

00:19:45.190 --> 00:19:48.520
They say those two don't even utter a word once they're in the theater!

00:19:48.520 --> 00:19:52.070
Casting the role with two actresses in the same role is the sort of sly move...

00:19:52.070 --> 00:19:54.510
we should expect from Daito.

00:19:56.770 --> 00:19:58.220
I'm really sorry!

00:19:58.220 --> 00:19:59.960
That's all right.

00:20:02.500 --> 00:20:06.470
They're laughing at me when I'm trying my hardest!

00:20:07.290 --> 00:20:10.120
There's still a huge gap between me and Ayumi.

00:20:10.120 --> 00:20:11.980
Maya.

00:20:11.980 --> 00:20:14.080
Sakurakouji!

00:20:14.080 --> 00:20:15.480
So you were here, after all.

00:20:15.950 --> 00:20:17.260
It's been a while, huh?

00:20:17.260 --> 00:20:18.600
Have you been well?

00:20:18.600 --> 00:20:20.570
How about you?

00:20:20.570 --> 00:20:21.800
You mean you thought about me?

00:20:21.800 --> 00:20:23.140
Of course I did!

00:20:23.860 --> 00:20:25.670
I hear you're playing Helen.

00:20:25.670 --> 00:20:27.720
Yeah! Both me and Ayumi.

00:20:27.720 --> 00:20:29.110
Yeah, that's what I heard.

00:20:34.060 --> 00:20:36.600
Catch you later!

00:20:36.600 --> 00:20:37.860
Maya...

00:20:39.510 --> 00:20:42.810
You say that as though we've made plans to see each other again.

00:20:42.810 --> 00:20:45.980
You really don't think about anything other than acting, do you?

00:20:48.290 --> 00:20:51.080
But, why?

